sec-channel-property-count: TPM_CAP_PUB_KEYS/TPM_CAP_SPDM_SESSION_INFO honor propertyCount

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, version 185, TPM2_GetCapability): "The
*propertyCount* parameter indicates the number of capabilities in the
indicated group that are requested. The TPM will return no more than the
number of requested values (*propertyCount*) or until the last property of
the requested type has been returned", and "The *moreData* parameter will have
a value of YES if there are more values of the requested type that were not
returned."

With SEC_CHANNEL_SUPPORT, the reference returns its TPM SPDM public key
(SpdmCapGetTpmPubKeys() ignores its count argument) and the entry of the
current SPDM session (SpdmCapGetSessionInfo() takes no count) even with
propertyCount = 0, with moreData = NO. The patch leaves the entry out and sets
moreData = YES in that case, like the reference's other capabilities (e.g.
PCRCapGetAllocation() for TPM_CAP_PCRS) and tpm-rs.
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Capability/GetCapability.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Capability/GetCapability.c
@@ -130,12 +130,30 @@
                 return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_GetCapability_property;
             out->moreData = SpdmCapGetTpmPubKeys(
                 (TPM_PUB_KEY)in->property, in->propertyCount, &data->pubKeys);
+            // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT
+            // determinism): the list holds "no more than the number of requested
+            // values (propertyCount)" (Part 3, TPM2_GetCapability), so with
+            // propertyCount = 0 the key is left out and reported by moreData.
+            // SpdmCapGetTpmPubKeys() ignores propertyCount.
+            if(in->propertyCount == 0 && data->pubKeys.count != 0)
+            {
+                data->pubKeys.count = 0;
+                out->moreData       = YES;
+            }
             break;
         case TPM_CAP_SPDM_SESSION_INFO:
             // Input property must be 0
             if(in->property != 0)
                 return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_GetCapability_property;
             out->moreData = SpdmCapGetSessionInfo(&data->spdmSessionInfo);
+            // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT
+            // determinism): as for TPM_CAP_PUB_KEYS, propertyCount bounds the
+            // list (SpdmCapGetSessionInfo() takes no count).
+            if(in->propertyCount == 0 && data->spdmSessionInfo.count != 0)
+            {
+                data->spdmSessionInfo.count = 0;
+                out->moreData               = YES;
+            }
             break;
 #  endif  // SEC_CHANNEL_SUPPORT
         case TPM_CAP_VENDOR_PROPERTY:
